or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py:1-12` — Preserve read-only plan-review status semantics. Consumer: MCP API maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_tool_offload.py:1-25` — Preserve that blocking tracker work is offloaded from the MCP event loop. Consumer: MCP maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_measurement_provenance_criterion.py:22-31` — Preserve measurement-provenance acceptance boundaries. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:1-13, 194-202` — Preserve mechanism-delta classification and shrink-only enforcement. Consumer: architecture-gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mirror_lock_terraform.py:1-16` — Preserve mirror-lock infrastructure ownership and configuration. Consumer: infrastructure maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py:1-19, 231-235, 261-268, 402-407` — Preserve model-class ordering, fallback, and configuration semantics. Consumer: LLM-runtime maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py:1-17, 63-66` — Preserve the locked module-size limit and enforcement wiring. Consumer: architecture-gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py:431-444, 539-542` — Preserve destructive-mutation confirmation and cancellation safety. Consumer: CLI safety maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py:1-9` — Preserve shrink-only mypy-baseline enforcement. Consumer: typecheck-gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_necessity_criterion.py:1-10` — Preserve necessity-criterion classification. Consumer: plan-review maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_network_fetch_stall_abort_851e.py:1-17` — Preserve abort behavior for stalled network fetches. Consumer: network-operation maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_network_guard_local_ipc.py:1-14` — Preserve local-IPC allowance without permitting external network access. Consumer: security and test-infrastructure maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_no_reducer_engine_support_cycle.py:1-14` — Preserve acyclic dependency direction between reducer, engine, and support modules. Consumer: architecture maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_no_stale_bare_review_cli.py:1-11` — Preserve absence of the retired bare review CLI. Consumer: CLI maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_no_verdict_obtainable_2a6f.py:1-15` — Preserve explicit handling when no gate verdict can be obtained. Consumer: gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_non_codebase_tag_edge.py:1-7` — Preserve non-codebase tag classification. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py:1-18` — Preserve rejection of operation certificates across untrusted environments. Consumer: security maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py:122-131, 361-364, 385-388` — Preserve secure key provisioning, permissions, and service wiring. Consumer: security and deployment maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts